  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1021 AM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nBelow normal temperatures will linger into next week. The\naforementioned upper low, unfortunately, is going to stall out\nover East Tennessee for much of next week, and that means low to\nmedium PoPs will stay with us throughout, mainly in areas east of\nI-65 and especially along the Cumberland Plateau. In fact, the \ntotal QPF from this afternoon through next Friday night shows \nquite the gradient as values range from less than 1/4\" along the \nTennessee River to 1 to 2\" across the Cumberland Plateau. So while\nthe risk of severe storms is extremely low after this evening, we\ncan't exactly look forward to dry week ahead. Temperatures will \nwarm back up to seasonal norms by week's end, but there are no \nheat-related concerns at this time.",
